    "pc_requirements": {
        "minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>OS *:</strong> Windows 10, 11 (untested on Windows 7 and 8 but ya know, it probably works)<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Intel i5 or Ryzen 5 3600<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 4 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> GTX 1050 (you probably can't run this on your momma's generic laptop)<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 4 GB available space<br></li><li><strong>Sound Card:</strong> Yeah probably have one of those<br></li><li><strong>VR Support:</strong> Nah, I fear that bunnies in VR might make things too real and the players would die of cuteness overload<br></li><li><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Look, I'll level with you, I'm a solo dev with marginal experience in optimization using a resource-hungry engine so you're going to need a mid-tier gaming computer if you want to keep up a good fps and visual fidelity.</li></ul>",
        "recommended": "<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> i7 or Ryzen 7<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> RTX 2060<br></li><li><strong>Sound Card:</strong> Put your head inside a tuba while your best friend goes crazy<br></li><li><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Make sure you have at least one controller if playing co-op!</li></ul>"
